section: compiler
issues: #20864 #22336 #25065 #27331
mrs: !16144
synopsis:
  Improve boxing of unboxed types with the new ``Box`` type
description:
  GHC sometimes needs to wrap an unboxed value with a data constructor in order
  to make it have kind ``Type``, which we call "boxing" the value. For example,
  GHC does this when compiling arrows, (parallel) list/monad comprehensions
  as well as recursive do statements.

  The internal machinery for doing so has been overhauled: GHC is now able to
  robustly box any type, instead of crashing (e.g. when compiling list/monad
  comprehensions). The main two issues fixed are:

    - GHC can now box types of any representation, including unboxed tuples,
      unboxed sums, ``AddrRep`` and all ``VecRep``s. This fixes #20864.
    - GHC can now box in the middle of typechecking, before the representation
      of the value to box has even been determined. This fixes #25065.
